<mxCell id="note_budgetgroup" parent="1" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=11;fontColor=#333333;fontStyle=2;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="budget_group_id NULL on a Transaction = the 'Others' bucket (FR-17). Not a row." vertex="1">
<mxGeometry height="90" width="190" x="1420" y="100" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="note_budgetperiod" parent="1" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=11;fontColor=#333333;fontStyle=2;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="start/end dates rather than a YYYY-MM key. A month is a calendar month (decided 2026-08-20); the date pair is kept anyway - it costs nothing, it is what a payday-to-payday model would need, and it makes quarterly and yearly rollups a date-range sum rather than a new column (NFR-3)." vertex="1">
<mxGeometry height="220" width="190" x="1420" y="220" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
